    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d169">

                <pb facs="0308" n="212" xml:id="pg212"/>

                <head>No. 169.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Edward Thornton to Mr.
                    Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-04-05"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 5, 1872</date>.
                        (Received April 9.)</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your letter of the 29th ultimo, relative to the facts which I was instructed
                    by Lord Granville to submit to you, with regard to the slave-trade on the east
                    coast of Africa, and I beg to offer you my best thanks for having acceded to the
                    wishes of Her Majesty’s government in this matter. I have forwarded a copy of
                    your note to Lord Granville, to whom I hope it will be satisfactory.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>EDWD. THORNTON.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
